<p>Local SEO is the difference between ranking for a search no one near you makes, and showing up the moment someone nearby searches for exactly what you offer. For most small businesses, this is where the fastest wins are.</p>

<h2>What's included</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Google Business Profile setup or full optimization</li>
  <li>Local citations and NAP consistency (name, address, phone across the web)</li>
  <li>Review strategy — getting more of them, responding to them properly</li>
  <li>Local keyword targeting (city, neighborhood, service-area terms)</li>
  <li>Location pages, where more than one service area is relevant</li>
</ul>

<p>This pairs especially well with a technical audit, since local ranking signals and on-site technical health reinforce each other.</p>
